# Shorts and Reels Blocker

Developer: VIKA-IN-TECH

A lightweight Chrome extension that blocks YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels, and Facebook Reels, so you can browse without falling into the endless scroll.

## What it blocks

- YouTube Shorts pages (youtube.com/shorts) - you get a "Blocked" page instead, with a Back button
- Instagram Reels (instagram.com/reels)
- Facebook Reels (facebook.com/reels)
- The Shorts shelf on the YouTube homepage, Shorts cards in search results, and the Shorts link in the sidebar
- The Reels tab on Instagram and Facebook

Shorts or Reels opened through in-app navigation (clicking inside YouTube or Instagram without a fresh page load) are caught by a content script as well.

## How it works

- declarativeNetRequest rules (rules.json) cancel network requests to Shorts/Reels URLs, so blocked pages never load.
- A content script (content.js) runs at document start and covers any Shorts/Reels page reached through single-page navigation with a "Blocked" screen.
- A CSS file (hide.css) hides the Shorts shelves, cards, sidebar links and Reels tabs so the temptation is gone, not just the destination.
- All blocking happens locally in your browser. No data is collected, nothing is sent anywhere.

## Install (Chrome, 3 steps)

1. Unzip this folder.
2. Open chrome://extensions in Chrome.
3. Turn on Developer mode (top right), click "Load unpacked", and select the unzipped shorts-reels-blocker folder.

Works in any Chromium browser (Chrome, Edge, Brave).

## Files

- manifest.json - extension config (Manifest V3, permissions, rules)
- rules.json - declarativeNetRequest blocklist for Shorts/Reels URLs
- content.js - catches in-app navigation to Shorts/Reels
- hide.css - hides Shorts/Reels shelves, tabs and cards
- blocked.html / blocked.js - the "Blocked" page you land on, with a Back button
- icons/ - toolbar and store icons

## Permissions

- declarativeNetRequest: to block Shorts and Reels requests.
- Host access to youtube.com, instagram.com, facebook.com: so the rules and hiding styles apply there.

Nothing else. No storage, no scripts, no network access of its own.

## Notes

- Version 1.0.0, Manifest V3.
- Uninstall anytime from chrome://extensions.
- Limitation: the sites redesign often, so if a Shorts shelf slips through after a YouTube update, the hiding CSS may need a small tweak.
